{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"callout","kind":"important","title":"Important","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you are using file-based routing, it's recommended to use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createLazyFileRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" function instead."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lazyRouteComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" function can be used to create a one-off code-split route component that can be preloaded using a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"component.preload()"},{"type":"text","value":" method."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"lazyroutecomponent-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"lazyRouteComponent options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lazyRouteComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" function accepts two arguments:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"importer-option","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"importer"},{"type":"text","value":" option"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => Promise<T>"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function that returns a promise that resolves to an object that contains the component to be loaded."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"exportname-option","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"exportName"},{"type":"text","value":" option"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The name of the component to be loaded from the imported object. Defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'default'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"lazyroutecomponent-returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"lazyRouteComponent returns"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"React.lazy"},{"type":"text","value":" component that can be preloaded using a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"component.preload()"},{"type":"text","value":" method."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { lazyRouteComponent } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/posts/$postId',\n  component: lazyRouteComponent(() => import('./Post')), // default export\n})\n\n// or\n\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/posts/$postId',\n  component: lazyRouteComponent(\n    () => import('./Post'),\n    'PostByIdPageComponent', // named export\n  ),\n})","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"lazyroutecomponent-options","text":"lazyRouteComponent options","level":2},{"id":"importer-option","text":"importer option","level":3},{"id":"exportname-option","text":"exportName option","level":3},{"id":"lazyroutecomponent-returns","text":"lazyRouteComponent returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> If you are using file-based routing, it's recommended to use the `createLazyFileRoute` function instead.\n\nThe `lazyRouteComponent` function can be used to create a one-off code-split route component that can be preloaded using a `component.preload()` method.\n\n## lazyRouteComponent options\n\nThe `lazyRouteComponent` function accepts two arguments:\n\n### `importer` option\n\n- Type: `() => Promise<T>`\n- Required\n- A function that returns a promise that resolves to an object that contains the component to be loaded.\n\n### `exportName` option\n\n- Type: `string`\n- Optional\n- The name of the component to be loaded from the imported object. Defaults to `'default'`.\n\n## lazyRouteComponent returns\n\n- A `React.lazy` component that can be preloaded using a `component.preload()` method.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { lazyRouteComponent } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/posts/$postId',\n  component: lazyRouteComponent(() => import('./Post')), // default export\n})\n\n// or\n\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/posts/$postId',\n  component: lazyRouteComponent(\n    () => import('./Post'),\n    'PostByIdPageComponent', // named export\n  ),\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: lazyRouteComponentFunction\ntitle: lazyRouteComponent function\n---\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> If you are using file-based routing, it's recommended to use the `createLazyFileRoute` function instead.\n\nThe `lazyRouteComponent` function can be used to create a one-off code-split route component that can be preloaded using a `component.preload()` method.\n\n## lazyRouteComponent options\n\nThe `lazyRouteComponent` function accepts two arguments:\n\n### `importer` option\n\n- Type: `() => Promise<T>`\n- Required\n- A function that returns a promise that resolves to an object that contains the component to be loaded.\n\n### `exportName` option\n\n- Type: `string`\n- Optional\n- The name of the component to be loaded from the imported object. Defaults to `'default'`.\n\n## lazyRouteComponent returns\n\n- A `React.lazy` component that can be preloaded using a `component.preload()` method.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { lazyRouteComponent } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/posts/$postId',\n  component: lazyRouteComponent(() => import('./Post')), // default export\n})\n\n// or\n\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/posts/$postId',\n  component: lazyRouteComponent(\n    () => import('./Post'),\n    'PostByIdPageComponent', // named export\n  ),\n})\n```\n"}
